# Forms — fieldops-app

All RHF / Zod usage goes through `core/integrations/form`. Features never import `react-hook-form`, `@hookform/resolvers`, or `zod` by package path.

## Required stack

- React Hook Form + Zod (brief). Create and edit share one form mode.
- UI fields from `core/integrations/ui` (`TextField`, `Select`, `Button`, …).

## Client rules (mirror mock-api)

- `title`: 8–120 characters
- `site`: required, non-empty
- `priority`: `low` | `medium` | `high` | `urgent`
- `dueAt`: valid date; if `priority` is `urgent`, due within 48 hours (cross-field)
- `checklist`: max 10 items; every item needs a non-empty label

Do **not** mirror undocumented server-only rules (e.g. title containing “asbestos”). Those arrive as 422 and map onto fields.

## Adapters

- `useAppForm` — typed RHF wrapper used by feature ViewModels.
- Schema builders / `z` re-exported from the form port.
- `applyServerFieldErrors(form, errorsMap)` — 422 `{ field: message }` → per-field `setError`. No toast-only path for field errors.
- Submit: disable control + loading while in flight; block double submit.
- Edit PATCH must send the loaded `version`.

## 409 conflict

Stale `version` returns 409 with `current` work order. Choose UX in `DECISIONS.md`. Hard rule: **never silently discard** what the technician typed.

## Keyboard

Focused field stays visible. Test checklist fields near the bottom of the form (KeyboardAvoidingView / scroll patterns as chosen at feature time).

## Accessibility

Labels and error text associated with inputs; disabled/loading states exposed via accessibility props.
